1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,090
Bunions - if the base of your big toe sticks out while the toe itself angles toward your other toes, here's why.

2
00:00:06,410 --> 00:00:10,097
Nearly one in four adults deals with this, and three habits speed it up.

3
00:00:10,417 --> 00:00:13,689
First, wearing high heels or narrow, pointed shoes often.

4
00:00:14,009 --> 00:00:21,709
Heel height shifts your weight onto the ball of your foot, and a tight toe box crowds your big toe inward - that's what makes the joint stick out more.

5
00:00:22,029 --> 00:00:24,418
Second, skipping toe and foot strengthening.

6
00:00:24,738 --> 00:00:29,763
The muscles holding your forefoot's arch weaken over time, so that crowding happens even faster.

7
00:00:30,083 --> 00:00:34,031
Third, brushing off that early ache or bump instead of changing anything.

8
00:00:34,351 --> 00:00:42,558
The tendons and ligaments around the joint tighten into that position the longer it's ignored, and once they adapt, footwear changes alone can't pull it back.

9
00:00:42,878 --> 00:00:47,293
Pick shoes with a wide toe box and a lower heel, and save heels for occasions.

10
00:00:47,613 --> 00:00:54,105
Toe-spreading stretches and towel-scrunch exercises daily keep that arch strong, and a toe spacer eases the pressure.

11
00:00:54,425 --> 00:00:56,996
See a podiatrist if it keeps getting worse.
